 <LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
     <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
+    <p><strong>General information &amp; Privacy by Design</strong></p>
+    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. At The DevTools Times, we follow <strong>Privacy by Design</strong>, <strong>Data Minimization</strong>, and <strong>User Transparency</strong> principles. We only collect the minimum data strictly necessary to provide the services you explicitly request.</p>
     
     <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
     <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
     <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
+    <p>Whenever you use this website, we limit data processing to essential functional operations. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect, how it is stored, and the specific purposes for which we use it.</p>
+
+    <h2>3. Account Registration and Sign-In (Data Minimization)</h2>
+    <p><strong>What we collect and why</strong></p>
+    <p>When you sign up or sign in to The DevTools Times, we only ask for a pseudonymous <strong>username</strong> and <strong>password</strong>. We do not require your real name, email address, phone number, or physical address. Your credentials are transmitted securely and used solely to authenticate your account and maintain your preferences. We do not sell, rent, or share your account data with third parties.</p>
     
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <h2>4. Recording of data on our website</h2>
+    <p><strong>Cookies &amp; Session Storage</strong></p>
+    <p>Our website uses strictly necessary first-party session cookies to provide core functionality you request, such as maintaining your bookmarked <strong>Reading List</strong> across pages. These cookies do not cause any damage to your computer, do not contain viruses, and are not used for cross-site tracking or behavioral profiling.</p>
+    <p><strong>Third-Party Scripts &amp; Tracking</strong></p>
+    <p>By default, third-party behavioral analytics and advertising tracking scripts are disabled across our pages to protect your privacy and browsing performance. Document headers such as <code>Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code> and a restrictive <code>Permissions-Policy</code> are enforced to prevent unauthorized access to browser features (such as camera, microphone, geolocation, and browsing topics) and minimize referrer leakage.</p>
+
+    <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
+    <p>You have the right to request information about your stored data, its origin, its recipients, and the purpose of its collection at any time, as well as the right to request the correction, portable export, or deletion of your account and personal data.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
